<!--Post: 2771--><!--Time: 1104101553-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2771"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 26, 2004 - 2:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ive never seen it posted as to where the lines were cut. Obviously if they were cut inside that would explain the lack of eyewitnesses to someone prowling. BUT if they were cut outside do we know where the phone lines ran to the houses &#40;side or back of the structure&#41;? They could have possibly been obscured by trees, shrubs, and shadows allowing him to sneak there by dodging amonst the shadows at night or early morning. If he took his time, and none of the neighbors had dogs to set off it could easily be done. He also could have snuck into the residence through a secluded darkened back entrance &#40;alot of older worn out locks can be picked with simple easily available tools&#41; and stayed there until the early morning, committing the murders THEN leaving, no disguise would ever be needed. <BR>If the lines were cut inside the house Id tend to think it was done just to prevent a call from going out.  <BR> <BR>Any thoughts on this theory?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2771-->
<!--Post: 2807--><!--Time: 1104161951-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2807"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 7:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I myself can only conclude that the lines were cut outside.  If one were to cut the lines outside it would disable the entire system.  Most homes have multiple phone jacks attached to the wall on the inside and are &#34;married&#34; in a junction box on the exterior.  Cutting the lines on the interior may only disable that particular phone, leaving the others, if any, fully operational.  Im not all that familiar with the utility practices of the day nor the age of the homes in question.  Im only saying what seems logigal to me. <BR> <BR>One quick sidebar, it is possible that he may have listened to their phone conversations through a linemans phone or splicing into the system.  This is very easily done by just about anyone with very little Comm knowledge.  By listening, he would have possibly gathered quite a bit of info from a victim including times they would be home alone or possible vistors.  Just my 2 cents!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2807-->
<!--Post: 2831--><!--Time: 1104175115-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2831"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 11:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think youre probably right about the lines being cut outside.  Makes me think he moved around out there in the dark either early morning or late night. The linesman phones you mentioned &#39;butt-sets&#39; would be logical, but maybe a bit bulky to carry, anything would be bulky if you need to get away quickly.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2831-->
<!--Post: 2967--><!--Time: 1104342921-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2967"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dawgar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dawgar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 9:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->January 1974  <BR> <BR> <BR>Victims&#39; children return home; clues sought  <BR> <BR>BY THE WICHITA EAGLE  <BR> <BR> <BR>Hannon said at the scene of the crime Tuesday that the mass slayings &#34;borders on a type of execution&#34; in that the telephone line leading into the home had been cut.  <BR> <BR>Feb. 11, 1978 <BR> <BR> <BR>Nancy Fox: Found slain Dec. 9, 1977 <BR> <BR>BY THE WICHITA EAGLE <BR> <BR>The phone had been taken off the hook and the lines had been cut on the outside of the house.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2967-->
<!--Post: 3021--><!--Time: 1104374531-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3021"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks for the info Dawgar...Makes me think even more that he was lurking outside before the murders...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3021-->
<!--Post: 3025--><!--Time: 1104375027-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3025"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why would someone take the phone off the hook if they&#39;d already cut the lines outside the house? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3025-->
<!--Post: 3027--><!--Time: 1104375479-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3027"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thats what I was wondering JuJuree.  Unless of course, depending on the time of day, she was on the phone while he snipped the lines.  She then went to investigate and he either met her at the door and forced his way in or waited and, this is quite popular, posed as a telephone repair man.  You know the rest.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3027-->
<!--Post: 3028--><!--Time: 1104375526-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3028"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Murco<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Murco<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->maybe someone tried to use it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3028-->
<!--Post: 3029--><!--Time: 1104375781-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3029"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 7:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Or maybe he took the phone off the hook, did his deed, then cut the lines on the way out.  Maybe an added insurance for a getaway.  Probably unlikely.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3029-->
<!--Post: 3030--><!--Time: 1104376109-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3030"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Moondog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Moondog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 7:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Taking the phone off the hook after cutting the phone line may seem redundant, but was probably part of BTK&#39;s signature or a message to LE.  Another explanation might be the victim&#40;s&#41; dropping the phone after attempting to call for help.  BTK probably took great pleasure in the victim&#39;s realization that the phone line had been cut and they were completely under his control - somewhat of a cat &amp; mouse game.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3030-->
<!--Post: 3031--><!--Time: 1104376279-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3031"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 7:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If the phone was indeed off the hook I can only think that the phone lines had been cut for awhile before she was killed.  Mind you, this is merely my speculation so bear with me please.  When the phone went out in our house because of storms or what have you, Dad would take the receiver off the hook.  That way he didnt have to constantly pick it up to see if there was a dial tone.  When service was restored the all too familiar buzzer would sound and that annoying operators voice.  Remember, &#34;If you&#39;d like to make a call....&#34;  Thats how we would know when the service was back up and running.  Maybe she did the same thing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3031-->
<!--Post: 3034--><!--Time: 1104376895-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3034"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 7:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think all your ideas are pretty good and very plausible. <BR> <BR>Secret squirrel, you just brought back some memories for me.  My father used to do the same thing if the phone went out.  That would have been in the 70&#39;s, too. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3034-->
<!--Post: 3035--><!--Time: 1104377549-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3035"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 7:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Its creepy how things start to tie in.  Its also truely amazing what we come up with when we all work together.  Good Job Everyone!!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3035-->
<!--Post: 3051--><!--Time: 1104385043-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3051"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dawgar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dawgar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 9:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->maybe she tried to make it to the phone when he suprised her and he never bothered to put the phone back on the hook knowing the line was cut anyway.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3051-->
<!--Post: 3064--><!--Time: 1104414452-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3064"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 5:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Definitely a very good possibility.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3064-->
<!--Post: 3080--><!--Time: 1104434550-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3080"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 11:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A struggle could have knocked it off also...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
